# Phase 12, second slice: Pane's window management. With the four demo
# windows up: Alt+Tab brings the next window to the top, Super+Left snaps
# it to the left half, Super+Up maximises it, Super+Down gives it its old
# place back, dragging the bottom-right corner of the top window resizes
# it and the program answers with a buffer of the new size. Keys typed
# for Pane are not replayed into the kernel desktop afterwards.
cerberus kernel shell
!send pane --demo
!wait 8
pane: screen
!keys alt tab
!wait 1
pane: alt-tab: window 3 on top
!keys meta_l left
!wait 1
pane: window 3 snapped left: 630x762 at 5,33
!keys meta_l up
!wait 1
pane: window 3 snapped maximised: 1270x762 at 5,33
!keys meta_l down
!wait 1
pane: window 3 restored: 280x160 at 144,152
!keys alt tab
!wait 1
pane: alt-tab: window 4 on top
!mouseto 494 342
!button left down
!mouse 100 60
!button left up
!wait 2
pane: window 4 resized: 420x220
pane: window 4 has a new 420x220 buffer
!keys ctrl alt q
!wait 3
pane: 
run: /bin/pane exited with status 0
!send gui
!wait 2
gui:
